      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The main issues for understandability:\n1. The class contains large unused data-provider methods and a helper method not used by this test\n2. Many unused imports clutter the file\n3. The expected values (`-1` seconds and `999999998` nanos) are not self-explanatory without understanding how `Duration` normalizes negative nanoseconds\n\nLet me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data-provider methods, the unused helper method, and all unused imports, leaving only the single focused test with a brief comment explaining why `-2ns` normalizes to `-1s + 999_999_998ns` in Java's `Duration` representation."
